## Agent dispatched

## Investigating cause 1 (RLS 42501 on [log-event])
- src/app/api/admin/log-event/route.ts:186-200 — used user-scoped supabase client to insert into admin_events. RLS migration (supabase/migrations/20260214220000_create_admin_events.sql:92-95) only allows INSERT to service_role.
- Fixed: switched to createAdminClient() inside POST after auth check.

## Investigating cause 2 (Refresh Token noise)
- src/proxy.ts:64 — updateSession() was not wrapped in try/catch (the older middleware.ts at repo root does wrap it). Stale-refresh-token AuthApiError bubbled out of supabase-js into the proxy.
- Fixed: src/proxy.ts now try/catches updateSession and downgrades refresh-token errors to console.warn.
- sentry.server.config.ts + instrumentation.ts — added "Invalid Refresh Token", "Refresh Token Not Found", "AuthApiError" to ignoreErrors so Sentry stops paging on normal session expiry.

## Investigating cause 3 (PGRST202 missing RPC for resend-activity stats)
- src/app/golf/actions/resend-activity.ts:149 — calls supabase.rpc('get_resend_activity_stats', { p_window }).
- src/app/golf/actions/resend-activity.ts:282 — calls supabase.rpc('get_resend_domain_breakdown', { p_window }).
- supabase/migrations/20260420000000_resend_activity_mirror.sql:333,415 — both RPCs are defined SECURITY DEFINER but the migration only does REVOKE EXECUTE FROM public, anon (lines 410, 458) and never GRANT EXECUTE TO authenticated. PostgREST returns PGRST202 "function not found" because the authenticated role has no execute privilege on the schema cache view.
- Decision: DB-side fix only — code call sites are correct. SQL grant block written into the SQL section.

## Investigating cause 4 (Error: [object Object] in golf/admin/page.js)
- Source of "Error: [object Object]": src/app/golf/actions/admin-data.ts:77 — `unstable_cache` body of `getAdminDashboardRollup`. When the wrapped RPC fails with a Supabase Postgrest error (plain object, not Error instance), `String(error)` coerced to the literal string "[object Object]". The cache wrapper rethrows that as Error("[object Object]"), and Next.js minified internals (J.tags / K.tags = cache-tag bookkeeping) surface it in the stack you see in production.
- Secondary: src/app/golf/actions/admin/rollup-a.ts:252 fallback `String(err)` returned "[object Object]" when JSON.stringify failed (circular ref / Symbol).
- Fixed: imported describeError() in admin-data.ts; replaced 4 String(e) sites with describeError(e). Hardened describeRpcError() in rollup-a.ts with circular-safe JSON serializer + extra fields (status, error_description, name, statusText) so the [object Object] fallback is no longer reachable.

## Investigating cause 5 (Stats timeout 57014)
- Source: src/app/golf/actions/stats-data.ts:825-861 — Promise.all([golf_holes select, golf_shots select with embedded putt_details/approach_miss_details]) using `.in('round_id', roundIds)`. When a player has many rounds (no preset filter applied) and many shots per round (90+ per round), Postgres hits statement_timeout (57014).
- Code-side decision: WONTFIX in this triage — the call site already swallows the timeout into `buildFallbackDetailedStats` (line 939) so user impact is graceful degradation. Long-term fix is to push the aggregation into a SQL function, but that's a larger refactor.
- DB-side recommendation: add covering index `idx_golf_shots_round_id_covering` and ensure FK indexes exist on putt_details(shot_id) / approach_miss_details(shot_id). SQL written below.

## Investigating cause 6 (fetch failed: expected non-null body source)
- Source: Next.js internal — node_modules/next/dist/esm/server/app-render/action-handler.js. The string "failed to forward action response" is emitted by Next.js when a server action's outgoing response body is null. This is a runtime/framework concern.
- Decision: WONTFIX from this triage. Verified no application-level fetch() in src/ passes body: null. The cause is Next.js 16's action-handler interacting with edge-cached responses; upstream issue, not actionable here.

## Investigating cause 7 (admin-data fetchAdminRollupA / get_admin_rounds_rollup)
- Source: src/app/golf/actions/admin/rollup-a.ts:288 calls supabase.rpc('get_admin_rounds_rollup', ...). The migration supabase/migrations/20260421000005_admin_rollups_a.sql:896 already does GRANT EXECUTE TO authenticated — function exists and is callable.
- The "[object Object]" log is the SAME bug as cause 4: describeRpcError() fell through to String(err) for a non-stringifiable error object. After the fix in cause 4, the next failure will surface the real Postgres code/message (most likely 57014 statement_timeout on the rollup, or auth.uid() being null).
- Code-side fix: same as cause 4 — circular-safe describeRpcError now extracts code/msg/details/hint/status/error_description even when JSON.stringify fails.
- Once visible, the underlying cause is most likely Postgres statement_timeout in the rollup body. SQL recommendation: bump statement_timeout for the SECURITY DEFINER function via ALTER FUNCTION ... SET statement_timeout. Written below.

