## Per-cause fix

### 1. RLS 42501 on [log-event]
- Source: src/app/api/admin/log-event/route.ts:186 (POST handler insert into admin_events).
- Root cause: Used `await supabase ...` (user-scoped client). RLS migration supabase/migrations/20260214220000_create_admin_events.sql:92-95 only allows INSERT to service_role; authenticated users have no INSERT policy → 42501.
- Fix applied: src/app/api/admin/log-event/route.ts — imported `createAdminClient`, switched the insert to the privileged admin client AFTER the existing user-auth check on line 145. Behaviour unchanged for unauthenticated users; authenticated user_id is still recorded on the row.

### 2. Refresh Token noise
- Source A: src/proxy.ts:64 — call to `updateSession()` was unwrapped (the older /middleware.ts at repo root already had try/catch, but the Next.js 16 proxy.ts did not).
- Source B: sentry.server.config.ts and instrumentation.ts — Sentry was capturing AuthApiError as a real "error", paging the team for normal session expiry.
- Fix applied:
  - src/proxy.ts: wrapped updateSession() in try/catch; refresh-token errors are downgraded to console.warn and the request continues with no session (legitimate logged-out state).
  - sentry.server.config.ts: added "Invalid Refresh Token: Refresh Token Not Found", "Refresh Token Not Found", "AuthApiError" to ignoreErrors.
  - instrumentation.ts: same ignoreErrors additions for both nodejs and edge runtime Sentry init.

### 3. Missing RPC (resend-activity)
- Source: src/app/golf/actions/resend-activity.ts:149 (`get_resend_activity_stats`) and :282 (`get_resend_domain_breakdown`).
- Root cause: supabase/migrations/20260420000000_resend_activity_mirror.sql defines both functions SECURITY DEFINER but only does `REVOKE EXECUTE FROM public, anon` (lines 410, 458). It NEVER `GRANT EXECUTE TO authenticated`. Without the grant, PostgREST omits the function from its schema cache → PGRST202 "Searched for the function public.<name>".
- Fix applied: code call sites are correct — function names match exactly. Fix is DB-side: GRANT EXECUTE on both functions (SQL written below).

### 4. Error: [object Object] on golf/admin/page.js
- Source A: src/app/golf/actions/admin-data.ts:77 — inside the `unstable_cache` body of `getAdminDashboardRollup`, line was `throw error instanceof Error ? error : new Error(String(error));`. Supabase Postgrest errors are plain objects (not Error instances), so `String(error)` returned the literal "[object Object]".
- Source B: src/app/golf/actions/admin/rollup-a.ts:252 — `describeRpcError` had a JSON.stringify-with-String-fallback. When the Supabase error contained circular references (very common: it nests itself in `cause`), JSON.stringify threw, the fallback ran `String(err)` → "[object Object]".
- Source C: src/app/golf/actions/admin-data.ts:1438, 1445, 1466, 1521-1522 — four sites used `e instanceof Error ? e.message : String(e)` which had the same toxic pattern when the upstream throw was already a wrapped Error("[object Object]").
- Fix applied:
  - src/app/golf/actions/admin-data.ts: imported `describeError` from `@/lib/utils/describe-error`, replaced 4 String(e) call-sites with `describeError(e)`, fixed line 77 to use `describeError(error)` so the Postgrest code/msg/details/hint are preserved when re-thrown out of the cache body.
  - src/app/golf/actions/admin/rollup-a.ts:239-279: hardened `describeRpcError` with a circular-safe JSON replacer (WeakSet) plus extra fields (status, statusText, error_description, name, error). Last-resort fallback now reports object key names instead of "[object Object]".

### 5. Stats timeout 57014
- Source: src/app/golf/actions/stats-data.ts:825-861 — Promise.all of `golf_holes` SELECT and `golf_shots` SELECT with embedded `putt_details` and `approach_miss_details` on `.in('round_id', roundIds)`. The IN list can be hundreds of rounds when the user has not selected a preset filter.
- Fix path: code already has a graceful catch (line 937-940) that falls back to round-level stats and logs the timeout as warning. The 9-per-day rate is acceptable degradation.
- DB-side recommendation: ensure FK indexes on putt_details(shot_id), approach_miss_details(shot_id), and a covering index on golf_shots for the SELECT shape. SQL written below; main agent should run `EXPLAIN ANALYZE` on the failing query and decide if a SQL function rewrite is worth the lift.

### 6. fetch failed: expected non-null body source
- Source: Next.js internal — node_modules/next/dist/esm/server/app-render/action-handler.js. Confirmed by grepping the framework source.
- No application code passes `body: null` to fetch().
- Decision: WONTFIX from this triage — framework-level bug, no fix exists in our codebase. 8/day occurrence is below alerting threshold.

### 7. fetchAdminRollupA / get_admin_rounds_rollup
- Source: src/app/golf/actions/admin/rollup-a.ts:288 → `rpc('get_admin_rounds_rollup', ...)`.
- Function definition exists and is granted: supabase/migrations/20260421000005_admin_rollups_a.sql:36 (function), :896-899 (GRANT EXECUTE TO authenticated).
- Same root cause as #4 — the RPC error message was lost inside `describeRpcError`. With the fix from #4, the next failure will surface the actual Postgres error code. Most likely candidate: 57014 statement_timeout on the rollup body itself (it has 17 sub-queries collapsed into 1; some windows may be slow under load).
- Fix applied: same code edit as #4 (rollup-a.ts describeRpcError hardening).
- Recommendation for main agent: bump statement_timeout for the SECURITY DEFINER rollup functions via `ALTER FUNCTION ... SET statement_timeout = '30s'`. SQL written below.

## SQL for main agent to apply
```sql
-- =============================================================================
-- Cause 3: Missing GRANT EXECUTE for resend-activity RPCs
-- File: supabase/migrations/20260420000000_resend_activity_mirror.sql
-- Lines 410, 458 do REVOKE FROM public, anon but never GRANT TO authenticated,
-- so PostgREST returns PGRST202 "function not found" for authenticated users.
-- =============================================================================
GRANT EXECUTE ON FUNCTION public.get_resend_activity_stats(text)    TO authenticated;
GRANT EXECUTE ON FUNCTION public.get_resend_domain_breakdown(text)  TO authenticated;

-- (The function bodies already enforce admin-role via auth.uid() check, so the
--  grant is safe — non-admins still receive `RAISE EXCEPTION 'Forbidden'`.)


-- =============================================================================
-- Cause 5: Stats timeout 57014 on detailed-stats query
-- File: src/app/golf/actions/stats-data.ts:825-861
-- The slow query is golf_shots SELECT with embedded putt_details +
-- approach_miss_details on `.in('round_id', roundIds)`.
-- =============================================================================

-- Ensure FK-side indexes exist on the embedded relationship sides.
-- (064_putt_approach_details.sql already creates these, but they may have been
-- dropped. IF NOT EXISTS makes this idempotent.)
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_putt_details_shot_id
  ON putt_details (shot_id);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_approach_miss_details_shot_id
  ON approach_miss_details (shot_id);

-- Covering index for the detailed-stats SELECT shape. Existing
-- idx_golf_shots_round_id is just (round_id); this version INCLUDEs the
-- columns the query actually returns so Postgres can serve the whole result
-- from the index without going to the heap.
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_golf_shots_round_id_covering
  ON golf_shots (round_id, hole_number, shot_number)
  INCLUDE (
    id, hole_id, shot_type, club_type,
    lie_before, lie_after, distance_to_hole_before, distance_unit_before,
    result, distance_to_hole_after, distance_unit_after, shot_distance,
    miss_direction, putt_break, putt_distance_feet, putt_slope, putt_made,
    is_penalty, penalty_type
  );

-- Optional: bump statement_timeout for the read-only stats path. Apply only
-- if the covering index alone doesn't bring p95 under the timeout threshold.
-- ALTER ROLE authenticated IN DATABASE postgres SET statement_timeout = '15s';


-- =============================================================================
-- Cause 7: fetchAdminRollupA timeouts on get_admin_rounds_rollup
-- File: supabase/migrations/20260421000005_admin_rollups_a.sql:36
-- The function is granted correctly. Failures are most likely 57014 timeout —
-- bump per-function statement_timeout so the SECURITY DEFINER body has more
-- runway than the global default.
-- =============================================================================
ALTER FUNCTION public.get_admin_rounds_rollup(
  timestamptz, timestamptz, timestamptz, timestamptz,
  timestamptz, timestamptz, timestamptz
) SET statement_timeout = '30s';

ALTER FUNCTION public.get_admin_users_rollup(
  timestamptz, timestamptz, timestamptz, timestamptz
) SET statement_timeout = '30s';

ALTER FUNCTION public.get_admin_feature_adoption_rollup(timestamptz)
  SET statement_timeout = '30s';

ALTER FUNCTION public.get_admin_coachhelm_rollup(
  timestamptz, timestamptz, timestamptz
) SET statement_timeout = '30s';
```

